---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/portfolio';
import { withBase } from '../lib/url';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy policy — Md Rakibul Hassan"
  description="How this website handles personal data: static hosting on GitHub Pages, no cookies, no analytics."
  path="privacy/"
  heading="Privacy policy"
  updated="Last updated: November 2026"
>
  <p>
    This is a static personal website. It sets no cookies, runs no analytics or tracking, embeds no
    third-party content and loads its fonts from this site, not from external servers. This policy
    explains the little data processing that does happen.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <p>
    {profile.name}, contact details and postal address as stated in the
    <a href={withBase('impressum/')} lang="de">
      Impressum
    </a>
    . Email:
    <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a>, phone:{' '}
    <a href={`tel:${profile.phoneHref}`}>{profile.phone}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Hosting on GitHub Pages</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc. (USA). When you open a page, your
    browser sends technical data that GitHub processes to deliver the site and keep it secure,
    typically your IP address, the date and time of the request, the requested URL, the referring
    page and your browser’s user agent. These server logs are under GitHub’s control; I have no
    access to them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. My legitimate interest is presenting this website reliably and
    securely. Processing by GitHub may involve a transfer of data to the USA. Details on GitHub’s
    processing and safeguards are in the
    <a
      href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
      rel="noopener noreferrer"
    >
      GitHub General Privacy Statement
    </a>
    .
  </p>

  <h2>3. No cookies, no analytics, self-hosted fonts</h2>
  <p>
    This site does not set cookies and does not use analytics, advertising or tracking tools. Fonts
    are delivered from this website itself, so no request is made to font providers such as Google
    Fonts.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Contacting me</h2>
  <p>
    If you contact me by email or phone, I process the data you provide (for example your name,
    email address and message) to answer your request. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where your
    message concerns a possible employment or contractual relationship, otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR
    (my legitimate interest in answering enquiries). I delete the data once it is no longer needed,
    unless statutory retention obligations apply.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>The contact form sends and stores nothing.</strong> When you press its button, your own
    email app opens with a pre-filled message. Nothing is transmitted to this website or to any
    third party; whether and how the message is sent is entirely up to you and your email provider.
  </p>

  <h2>5. External links and downloads</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to external websites such as GitHub and LinkedIn. They are only contacted if you
    follow a link; from then on, the provider’s own privacy policy applies. Downloading the CV (PDF)
    is a plain file request to GitHub Pages, processed as described in section 2.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access the personal data I hold about you (Art. 15);</li>
    <li>have it corrected (Art. 16) or erased (Art. 17);</li>
    <li>restrict its processing (Art. 18);</li>
    <li>receive it in a portable format (Art. 20);</li>
    <li>object to processing based on Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (Art. 21).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To exercise these rights, contact me using the details in section 1.</p>

  <h2>7. Right to lodge a complaint</h2>
  <p>
    You can complain to a data protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR). The authority
    responsible for me is the Hessian Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information
    (HBDI):
    <a href="https://datenschutz.hessen.de" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      datenschutz.hessen.de
    </a>
    .
  </p>
</Legal>
